     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"padding-bottom:20px;width:1032px;font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:medium\"><div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px;direction:ltr;margin-top:8px\"><div style=\"overflow:hidden;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-stretch:normal;font-size:small;line-height:1.5;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I am using tidyLPA to run my data. To select the number of profiles, I ran the BLRT. It seems like all the loglikehood values resulted from tidyLPA are positive (also looked at the papers that have cited tidyLPA). Are the values set to be positive by default?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks</div><div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div></div><div></div></div></div><div style=\"border-bottom-left-radius:1px;border-bottom-right-radius:1px;width:auto;background:rgb(242,242,242)\"></div></div></div></div>"
